ne 500", "year": 2023, "rank": 98, "itemDescription": "The producer of processors, modems, platforms, and other connected components faced macroeconomic challenges in the semiconductor industry. It began 2023 with a hiring freeze and other cost-cutting efforts in place.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>The company\u2019s $44 billion in revenue in 2022 was a $32% increase from 2021. It rose nine places on the Fortune 500 this year.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>CEO Cristiano Amon has expressed confidence in Qualcomm\u2019s ability to invest in areas that will deliver long-term value, such as A.I.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>In May 2023, Qualcomm announced plans to acquire Autotalks, a chipmaker that builds semiconductor and system-on-a-chip technology for vehicle safety. As part of the deal, Qualcomm plans to integrate Autotalks\u2019 communication tech into its Snapdragon Digital Chassis portfolio, which features cloud-connected automotive platforms.</li><br />\r\n</ul>"}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2022, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "global500", "title": "Fortune Global 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 429, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2022, "rank": 5, "itemDescription": "<p class=\"p1\">As cars grow more and more like iPads on wheels, Qualcomm\u2019s tech has become central to making them cleaner and safer. Its Snapdragon Digital Chassis platform helps synchronize internal electronics to make combustion engines more fuel-efficient. In newer cars, Snapdragon coordinates the systems that underpin collision-avoidance systems\u2014and will soon empower self-driving.<span class=\"Apple-converted-space\">\u00a0</span></p>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2022, "rank": 107, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2021, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2021, "rank": 124, "itemDescription": "Qualcomm creates digital telecom products and services, including wireless semiconductors and software, and owns patents critical to 5G and 4G mobile communications standards. On July 1, company veteran Cristiano Amon will become CEO as Steve Mollenkopf is stepping down after more than two decades with the company. And Amon is coming in at a time when business is booming with the promise of 5G to provide powerful computing power to billions of devices."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2020, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 126, "itemDescription": "The San Diego-based company, which was founded in 1985, designs and manufactures digital telecom products and services. It has been an early leader in making products for the evolving 5G connectivity market."}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2020, "rank": 26, "itemDescription": "Qualcomm\u2019s chips are central to the infrastructure of the ultrafast wireless networks dubbed 5G. While carriers are only in early stages of deployment, some potential benefits of these 5G networks are already appearing in trial projects. Among them: fatality-reducing \u201csmart\u201d traffic control with sensors embedded in roads and signals, and targeted agriculture that uses far less water and fertilizer."}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2019, "rank": null, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 137, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "change-the-world", "title": "Change the World", "year": 2019, "rank": 1, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "worlds-most-admired-companies", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "year": 2018, "rank": null, "itemDescription": "